   "source": {
    "label": "th:two-arms",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For the two-armed stochastic bandit problem ($N=2$), Thompson Sampling algorithm has expected regret $$\\Ex[{\\cal R}(T)] = O\\left(\\frac{\\ln T}{\\Delta}+\\frac{1}{\\Delta^3}\\right)$$ in time $T$, where $\\Delta = \\mu_1-\\mu_2$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Regret defined as sum_i Delta_i E[k_i(T)] (pseudo-regret). Proof gives explicit bound 40 ln T/Delta + 48/Delta^3 + 18 Delta. Holds also for Bernoulli TS (Algorithm 1). Algorithm does not use T, so anytime. Unique optimal arm assumed WLOG (Appendix A)."
  },
